    {
      question: 'What is wayfinding and why do I need it?',
      answer: 'Wayfinding (also called signage or orientation system) encompasses all visual elements that serve orientation in buildings and on premises: directional signs, door signs, floor plans, pictograms, directional arrows and digital information systems. Good wayfinding guides visitors intuitively to their destination, reduces inquiries to staff and conveys professionalism. Particularly important in hospitals, hotels, office buildings, shopping centers and public buildings.',
